{"id":"e5ce25d74996e696","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-df-zfc-chain-union.md","title":"ZFC Chain Union","display":"df-zfc-chain-union — ZFC Chain Union","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-chain-union","aliases":["58-df-zfc-chain-union"],"display":"df-zfc-chain-union — ZFC Chain Union","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[58-df-chain]]","[[58-df-union]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-chain-union"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-chain-union</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-chain-union — ZFC Chain Union"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"a07664003abe8d32\" href=\"?note=a07664003abe8d32\" title=\"58-df-chain\">58-df-chain</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5a295a90caf70085\" href=\"?note=5a295a90caf70085\" title=\"58-df-union\">58-df-union</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I,M,\\vec M,B\\in V\">\\(I,M,\\vec M,B\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"i,j\\in I\">\\(i,j\\in I\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Chain}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{Chain}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"a07664003abe8d32\" href=\"?note=a07664003abe8d32\" title=\"58-df-chain\">58-df-chain</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ChainUnion}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ChainUnion}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}chain\\text{-}union} \\vdash \\mathrm{ChainUnion}_S(M,\\vec M)\\leftrightarrow\\exists I,B,P\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\vec M,I,B)\\land P=\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec M)\\land\\operatorname{Chain}(P,P,\\subseteq\\cap(P\\times P))\\land M=\\bigcup P\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}chain\\text{-}union} \\vdash \\mathrm{ChainUnion}_S(M,\\vec M)\\leftrightarrow\\exists I,B,P\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Function}(\\vec M,I,B)\\land P=\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec M)\\land\\operatorname{Chain}(P,P,\\subseteq\\cap(P\\times P))\\land M=\\bigcup P\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Auxiliary ZFC definition.</li>\n<li>The index set is recovered from a set-coded function, and the chain order is fixed to inclusion on its actual range. The former existentially arbitrary carrier and relation made every family a “chain” under a suitable degenerate choice.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"r